## What was produced

**1. Transcripts — 173 files, all media converted.** Every mp4/mp3 (104
  hours of audio across the three folders) now has a sibling
  `*.transcript.md`, generated with the knowledge_base whisper flow
  (faster-whisper large-v3, CUDA float16, beam 5, auto language-detect for
  the Cantonese), sped up with batched inference + VAD — ran at ~30x
  realtime, so the whole corpus took ~3.5h with zero failures. Lesson PDFs
  and docx files were also extracted to markdown (37 + 2 files). Media
  transcripts use a `.transcript.md` suffix so they never collide with the
  PDF extracts that share the same filename.

**2. Nine single-file course syntheses** (`course_synthesis.md` in each
  course folder), each capturing all frameworks, rules, numbers, trade
  examples and stories, with marketing/logistics/filler stripped, plus a
  rules quick-reference appendix and a lesson-map appendix:

| Course | Size |
|---|---|
| Big Picture Trading (one course) | ~65k words / 403KB — 6 parts:
  macro/money, options foundations, strategy playbook, gold options, risk &
  crash playbook, platforms/tools |
| J Law超績投資客 (one course) | 131KB, written in 繁體中文（香港用語) — 12 chapters incl.
  the four rule-books reproduced in full and the MRA template described |
| Real Vision ×7 | The Real Investing Course (111KB, 31 lessons), My Life in
  4 Trades (210KB, all 15 guest episodes), Imran Lakha options (86KB),
  Business Cycle (63KB), Peter Brandt (63KB), Tom DeMark (55KB), Dave Floyd
  (49KB) |

Quality notes: where Real Vision provided human-made PDF transcripts I used
  those as the primary source and skipped the duplicate whisper text;
  obvious speech-to-text garble (names like "Pierre Anderon"→Andurand,
  homophones in the Cantonese) was fixed from context, and genuinely
  unrecoverable names are marked rather than invented.

**Loose end:** `Real Vision/Research_ How the Pros Do It - Jared Dillian and
  Tony Greer` is a standalone podcast, not part of any course — transcribed
  but not synthesized.

**Reusable tooling** left in `external_references/`: `transcribe_all.py` and
  `extract_pdfs.py` (both idempotent — they skip already-done files, so you
  can drop in new videos and re-run; they run via the knowledge_base venv),
  and `SYNTHESIS_BRIEF.md`, the keep-everything/drop-marketing brief the
  synthesis passes follow.

